<title>USA: Zebra Technologies Q4 net up on improved margins.</title>
<headline>Zebra Technologies Q4 net up on improved margins.</headline>
<dateline>VERNON HILLS, Ill. 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zebra Technologies Corp said Tuesday improved margins helped the company post higher earnings in the fourth quarter ended December 31.</p>
<p>The bar code label manufacturing company reported net income of $8.7 million, or $0.36 a share, compared to $7.9 million, or $0.33 a share, one year ago.</p>
<p>Revenues were $47.1 million, versus $41.2 million.</p>
<p>Zebra said the 1996 figures include a pre-tax charge of $315,000, or about $0.01 a share, related to failed merger discussions with Eltron International Inc.</p>
<p>Zebra shares closed down 1/4 Tuesday at 24-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
